Apply the MSVC C runtime mode of a linking target to its whole configuration.

A toolchain can select the CRT mode only from `--features`, for each configuration. The MSVC toolchain of `@llvm`
does, and it builds one libc++ archive for each configuration in that mode. So `features = ["static_link_msvcrt"]` on
a `cc_binary`, a `cc_shared_library` or a `cc_test` does not change its link: the target still imports the dynamic C
runtime.

Give the three linking rules a transition. When the `features` of the target hold `static_link_msvcrt`, it adds
`static_link_msvcrt` and `-dynamic_link_msvcrt` to `--features`, so the whole dependency graph of the target takes the
static CRT. A target without the feature keeps its configuration.
